## New Direction: Unified Content System

After Myah's feedback, the content architecture is being restructured:

### ONE "New Post" button creates everything

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| Title | Content title |
| Type | Post / Guide / Review (dropdown) |
| Tags | Organic hashtag system (auto-suggest) |
| Links | YouTube URL, social media URL (optional) |
| Excerpt | Short summary |
| Content | TipTap editor |
| Status | Draft / Published / Hidden |

### Tag System (Like Hashtags)

- Tags created automatically when Myah types new ones
- Auto-suggest shows existing tags while typing
- Prevents spelling duplicates
- Visitors filter feed by clicking tags
- Tag list grows organically as she posts

### Homepage Feed

- Endless scroll (already built)
- Filter buttons replace tabs: All / Posts / Guides / Reviews
- Tag chips for additional filtering
- Sort options: Date / Tag / Type
- Each card shows type + tags + optional link

### No More Separate Tabs

- /blog, /guides, /reviews tabs REMOVED
- Everything on homepage feed
- Filters handle organisation

